hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19219","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abu Masud meaning al-Jurayri from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Maiz from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah alone, then jihad, then an accepted Hajj, surpassing the rest of deeds as between the rising of the sun and its setting."
"19220","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Hayyan ibn Umayr, Maiz narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He mentioned similar to it."
